Dear all

Due to the different method we approaach the topics and fyp project in MUM, the final proposal slide deck needs minor changes to reflect them properly and still map to the rubrics accordingly

For your final presentation, your slides should have the following content (which maps to the marking breakdown in the worksheet)

Slide No.1 - Project name, team ID, member names, supervisor name

Slide No.2 - Problem/opportunity statement : what are you trying to solve? what are you trying to acheive? what is out there that does not work/deliver/has flaws that you want to improve upon?

Slide No.3 - Project goals : what do you intend to deliver?

Slide No.4 - Major finalised (for now) project requirements : what do you need to complete to satisfy goals (e.g. function A,B,C, along with deployment on D to deliver on the goal of developing mobile app for X). There is NO strict requirement of 5 because this depends on topic complexity and supervisor demands - although there should be enough to qualify the project as one that needs multiple people working on it .....  a project with only 1 or 2 requirements typically only needs 1 developer.

Slide No.5 - Project stakeholders and end users : who benefits from the goals?

Slide No.6 - WBS

Slide Nos.7-9 - Software design of main portions of the project : minimally UI/UX walkthrough of a proposed GUI for the project is needed highlighting where the project goals/requirements are mapped to. Optionally any important software design vital for the success of the project (e.g. proposed ERD for data-centric projects, proposed system architecture for server/client based deployments, OOP/class diagrams for algorithm projects etc)

Slide No.10 - updated/correct/latest timeline of project (Gantt chart)

Slide No.11 - what is expected to be in scope and must be completed (to satisfy 3 and 2 above), what will be out of scope

Slide No.12 - what forseeable challenges does the team think they will face

Slide No.13 - what part of effective teamwork the team has experienced as of this phase OR what is missing and should be improved upon in upcoming phases

Slide No.14 - what part of effective project management the team has experienced as of this phase OR what is missing and should be improved upon in upcoming phases

As usual, hold discussions with your team supervisor to discuss what is best to fit into each slide, complete the deck and upload onto Moodle here for sign off from your supervisor (same process as before)

